    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d156">

                <pb facs="0214" n="202" xml:id="pg202"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/3176</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Netherlands Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Loudon</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2840</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-05-16">May 16, 1940</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform Your Excellency
                    that I have received a telegraphic communication from the Netherlands Minister
                    in London, informing me that Her Majesty Queen Wilhelmina and the Netherlands
                    Government are for the time being in London<anchor n="64" xml:id="d156-f1"/> and
                    that in the greater part of The Netherlands the Netherlands Army has laid down
                    arms.</p>
                <p>The Netherlands, however, remain to be in a state of war with Germany and
                    consequently the Netherlands Navy and the armed forces operating in those parts
                    of The Netherlands, which have not been occupied, will continue to fight.</p>
                <p>Please accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>A. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Loudon</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d156-f1" n="64" xml:id="d156-f1-content">
                <p>On August 10, 1940, It. E. Schoenfeld was designated to perform duties as
                    American Chargé near the Netherlands Government at London.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
